OracleAdapter.setPriceFeeds

when called by the owner with valid, equal-length arrays
    it sets priceFeeds for all tokens
        expect priceFeeds[token[i]] to equal feeds[i] for each i
    it sets heartbeats for all tokens
        expect heartbeats[token[i]] to equal heartbeat[i] for each i
    it emits PriceFeedSet event with the provided arrays
        expect event with (tokens, feeds, heartbeat)

when updating existing entries
    it overwrites previous feed and heartbeat values
        expect mappings updated to new values

when arrays have different lengths
    it reverts
        expect revert with Errors.LengthMismatch

when any token or feed address is zero
    it reverts 
        expect revert with ZeroAddress and does not change any state

when any heartbeat value is zero
    it reverts
        expect revert with ZeroAmount and does not change any state

when called by a non-owner
    it reverts
        expect revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount including the caller
